preConditionHook:
// CHOP, MEASURED BY CROSSINGS: price has crossed the moving average at least
// maxCrosses times inside the last lookback bars. Both sides identical --
// chop has no direction.
//
// Not TightRangeBlocksEntries, which shares the ROLE and the intent but
// measures how TALL the last N bars are; the two disagree on a wide slow
// range and on a tight trending drift.
//
// DIVERGENCE FROM THE BOOK, recorded rather than hidden: the generator's
// Switch role both blocks entries AND forces an exit on the same side, while
// Grimes asks only for the block. There is no block-without-flat role. If
// forcing flat is not wanted, place this rule NEGATED in each entry pane
// instead -- the same divergence TightRangeBlocksEntries records.
//
// No book number for "chopping back and forth": 4 crossings in 20 bars is a
// chosen starting point and both are optimizer inputs.
// MultiWalk's WFSafe_Xaverage, the function the EasyLanguage twin calls,
// ported unchanged from EmaGapBar / EmaSlope (the EMA references, which carry
// the full measurements). From EL_XAverage_Probe.txt (@OJ 240min, two chart
// starts):
//   * the wrapper is BIT-IDENTICAL to the plain XAverage built-in at a fixed
//     length -- (wf - xa) * 1e12 printed exactly 0.0000 on all 17,785 bars;
//   * the SEED is the PRICE on the study's first calculated bar
//     (ctx.CurrentBar() == 1), not a length-term simple average;
//   * the recurrence is x + sf*(p - x), ONE statement, never sf*p + (1-sf)*x:
//     the two separated on 67% of probed bars past 100. Do not re-associate;
//   * there is NO warm-up hole on the CURRENT value, so no bar-count guard
//     returning 0;
//   * an EMA NEVER FORGETS ITS SEED -- it decays at (1 - sf)^n, ~330 bars --
//     so Max Bars Back and the chart start are part of this rule's spec.
// LENGTH CHANGE MEASURED 2026-09-17 (EL_XAverage_Lag_Probe.txt): the wrapper
// recomputes sf on the bar the length changes and carries its state, no
// re-seed, so the length may be optimized in grids.
// Scratch is declared in localVariables, never at hook scope: the generator
// only prefixes declared locals, so a hook-scope declaration is a
// redefinition when the rule is placed twice in one strategy.
emaSf = 2.0 / (maLength + 1.0);
if (ctx.CurrentBar() == 1) {
    emaVal = close[0];
} else {
    emaVal = emaVal + emaSf * (close[0] - emaVal);
}
// The EMA's own lagged history, mirrored as a zero-seeded ring buffer and
// re-seeded if the depth changes, exactly as EmaSlope does. MEASURED: a
// series function's [k] is bit for bit the value it printed k bars earlier,
// and BEFORE that history exists the read is 0.0 -- not the seed, not a
// sentinel. Depth lookback + 1 covers lags 0..lookback.
emaDepth = (int)lookback + 1;
if (emaDepth < 2) {
    emaDepth = 2;
}
if (emaHistory.size() != (std::size_t)emaDepth) {
    emaHistory.assign((std::size_t)emaDepth, 0.0);
    emaCursor = 0;
}
emaHistory[emaCursor] = emaVal;
emaCursor = (emaCursor + 1) % emaHistory.size();
crossCount = 0;
for (ii = 0; ii < (int)lookback; ++ii) {
    aboveNow = el_gt(close[ii], emaHistory[(emaCursor + emaHistory.size() - 1 - (std::size_t)ii) % emaHistory.size()]);
    abovePrev = el_gt(close[ii + 1], emaHistory[(emaCursor + emaHistory.size() - 2 - (std::size_t)ii) % emaHistory.size()]);
    if (aboveNow != abovePrev) {
        crossCount = crossCount + 1;
    }
}
// THE WARM-UP GUARD IS LOAD-BEARING, not hygiene: the mirrored EMA history
// reads 0.0 on the first ii evaluated bars, and close[ii] > 0 is a SIGN TEST
// ON A PRICE. These series are back-adjusted futures -- a price may
// legitimately be negative or zero -- so that comparison would manufacture
// crossings out of the roll offset and the rule would fail the shift test.
chopReady = ctx.CurrentBar() > (int)lookback;
